# satpulsewb with no -L: the real default-port path (the canonical port, or an
# OS-picked fallback when it is taken), an all-interfaces bind, and a generated
# access token -- the URL and token the runner parses from stdout. -n keeps the
# guided path from opening a browser on the test host. -d with -s auto-connects at
# startup over the read-only FIFO the runner allocated, so the session skips
# probing, falls to passive detection, and still reaches connected.
-v
-n
-d
${SATPULSE_TEST_SERIAL}
-s
38400
